# This file is written automatically by `npx convex dev` — you normally do NOT
# edit it by hand. It is shown here only to document what ends up in
# packages/backend/.env.local. .env.local is gitignored.

# Set by `convex dev`:
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
CONVEX_URL=
CONVEX_SITE_URL=

# No Clerk vars belong in this file. The Convex *deployment* env is a separate
# store, and it is where Clerk's values must go:
#   CLERK_FRONTEND_API_URL        (for convex/auth.config.ts — from
#                                  https://dashboard.clerk.com/apps/setup/convex)
#   CLERK_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET  (for convex/http.ts — the webhook's signing secret)
# Set both with `npx convex env set …`; verify with `npx convex env list`.

# Didit identity verification belongs in the same *deployment* env, for the same
# reason: convex/identity.ts and convex/http.ts read process.env on the
# deployment, and `convex dev` does not push this file into it.
#   DIDIT_API_KEY                 (for convex/identity.ts `startSession` — the
#                                  API key from https://business.didit.me)
#   DIDIT_WEBHOOK_SECRET          (for convex/http.ts `/didit-webhook` — the raw
#                                  HMAC-SHA256 secret. Didit does NOT use Svix,
#                                  so this is not a whsec_… Clerk-style secret.)
#   DIDIT_WORKFLOW_ID             (optional — which verification workflow to run)
#   DIDIT_API_URL                 (optional — override the session endpoint;
#                                  defaults to Didit's hosted v2 URL)
# Set them with `npx convex env set …`; verify with `npx convex env list`.
# In the Didit dashboard, point the webhook at
#   https://<your-deployment>.convex.site/didit-webhook
